cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: hotspot-preflight
abstract: >-
  A preflight checker for de novo protein binder design. Given a target
  structure and the hotspot residues a designer intends to target, it reports
  whether those residues are actually modelled in the deposited coordinates,
  whether they remain solvent-exposed on the biological assembly rather than
  only on a truncated construct, and whether they are expressed in the residue
  numbering scheme the downstream design tool expects. It sits in front of
  tools such as BindCraft, RFdiffusion and BoltzGen, which take hotspot
  residues as user input and do not validate them.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
